    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "phy9-c2-s6-n124",
        "text": "磁通量\n\n要精确、定量地表述法拉第电磁感应定律，需要引入一个新的物理量：**磁通量**。\n\n考虑放在匀强磁场中的平面闭合导线，也就是一个平面回路，回路面积为 $S$。\n回路平面的法线 $\\vec{n}$ 与磁感应强度 $\\vec{B}$ 的夹角为 $\\alpha$（图 283）。\n\n**磁感应强度的大小、面积 $S$ 和 $\\vec{B}$ 与 $\\vec{n}$ 的夹角 $\\alpha$ 的余弦三者的乘积，称为通过面积 $S$ 的磁通量 $\\Phi$**：\n$\\Phi=BS\\cos\\alpha$。\n（12-1）\n\n图　283\n\n乘积 $B\\cos\\alpha=B_n$ 是磁感应强度在回路平面法线方向上的投影。\n因此，磁通量也可以写为：\n$\\Phi=B_nS$。\n\n（12-2）\n\n磁感应强度 $\\vec{B}$ 描述空间中每一点的磁场。\n磁通量不仅取决于 $\\vec{B}$，还取决于回路的面积，以及回路相对于磁力线的取向。\n\n磁通量可以用穿过面积 $S$ 的磁力线作有向计数来解释，计数的正负以选定的回路平面法线方向为准。\n如果约定，穿过垂直于矢量 $\\vec{B}$ 的单位面积的磁力线数目等于矢量的大小 $B$，并将沿选定法线方向穿过的磁力线计为正、反向穿过的计为负，那么磁通量就等于穿过面积 $S$ 的磁力线的有向计数。\n反转选定的法线方向会使磁通量反号；\n\n在这里的匀强磁场和平面回路条件下，不区分穿过方向的几何计数只对应磁通量的大小，不随法线方向的反转而改变。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy9-c2-s6-n124",
        "text": "Magnetic Flux\n\nTo state Faraday's law of electromagnetic induction precisely and quantitatively, we need a new physical quantity: **magnetic flux**.\n\nConsider a plane closed wire loop in a uniform magnetic field. Its area is $S$.\n\nThe normal $\\vec{n}$ to the plane of the loop and the magnetic induction $\\vec{B}$ make an angle $\\alpha$ (Figure 283).\n\n**The product of the magnitude of the magnetic induction, the area $S$, and the cosine of the angle between $\\vec{B}$ and $\\vec{n}$, denoted by $\\alpha$, is called the magnetic flux through the area $S$ and is denoted by $\\Phi$**.\n\nThe magnetic flux is given by the following expression:\n$\\Phi=BS\\cos\\alpha$. (12-1)\n\nFigure 283\n\nThe product $B\\cos\\alpha=B_n$ is the projection of the magnetic induction onto the normal to the plane of the loop.\nThe magnetic flux can therefore also be written as follows:\n$\\Phi=B_nS$. (12-2)\n\nThe magnetic induction $\\vec{B}$ describes the magnetic field at each point in space.\n\nMagnetic flux depends not only on $\\vec{B}$, but also on the area of the loop and its orientation relative to the magnetic field lines.\n\nMagnetic flux can be interpreted as a directed count of magnetic field lines passing through the area $S$, with signs defined relative to the chosen normal to the plane of the loop.\n\nSuppose that the number of magnetic field lines crossing a unit area perpendicular to the vector $\\vec{B}$ is defined to equal the vector's magnitude $B$, with crossings along the chosen normal counted positively and crossings against it counted negatively.\n\nUnder this convention, magnetic flux equals the directed count of magnetic field lines passing through the area $S$.\n\nReversing the chosen normal reverses the sign of the flux. In the uniform-field, plane-loop case considered here, a geometrical count that ignores crossing direction corresponds only to the magnitude of the flux and does not change when the chosen normal is reversed."
      }
    ],
